While supporting ongoing response operations in the Caribbean following the impacts of Hurricane Melissa, the PDC team is also supporting partners in the Pacific in response to Typhoon Kalmaegi and the recently formed Tropical Depression 32W.

Typhoon Kalmaegi, referred to locally as “Tino”, brought heavy flooding and significant damage to parts of the central Philippines, and is forecast to move westward toward central Vietnam over the next few days.

Another system, currently designated Tropical Depression 32W, has formed near Yap, Micronesia. Forecast models suggest it could track west-northwestward, potentially approaching the northern Philippines by early next week as a powerful typhoon.’

